  "prefLabel": "En 1804.01 Energy Code Compliance",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1804.01 Energy Code Compliance.\n\n(a) In accordance with RSA 155-A:10-a, applicants who intend to construct new or alter existing residential buildings in municipalities without an adopted code enforcement mechanism, shall submit a completed application to the department on behalf of the BCRB for verification that the proposed applicable project meets the energy code requirements.\n\n(b) An applicant shall demonstrate that a proposed residential building subject to the requirements of the energy code meets or exceeds the minimum construction standards of the energy code pursuant to RSA 155-A.\n\n(c) No project shall be considered approved pursuant to En 1800 and RSA 155-A without the issuance of a verification letter by the department.\n\nSource. #14381, eff 9-22-25, EXPIRES: 9-22-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1800.html"
